# Truth Collective

Read `docs/TC-STANDING-BRIEF.md` and `STAGING-RECOVERY-HANDOFF.md` before acting.

## Hard rules
- Staging only unless Daniel explicitly asks for live work. Live path is `public_html` without `tcstaging`. Never Website backup restore for staging recovery.
- No guessing. If below ~99% certainty, stop and say so.
- Do not rename/merge/delete locked classes: `tc-book-card`, `tc-product-card`, `tc-leadership-body`, `tc-book-button`, `tc-card-row`, `tc-overlay-card`, `tc-overlay-card-product`, `tc-explore-hub`, `tc-grade-block`, `tc-rating`, `tc-tech-intro`, `tc-explore-hero`.
- Do not change published/indexed slugs.
- Content Cursor touches: no em dashes, no bold body, no contractions, no hype/clickbait.
- Affiliate-only product mentions. Leave 10WEB manager alone until Daniel asks.
- Angie: only Cursor-written one-task prompts (`diagnostics/ANGIE-CONTROL.md`). Prefer Plan/Approve.
- Fix cause; do not invent parallel CSS systems. Prefer Vercel-style readable overlays from the standing brief §1. Aim lighter/less bulky than current staging without copying TechRadar’s commercial news look.
- **Additional CSS:** only Cursor + Daniel. Claude may advise aesthetics/format and write specs for Cursor; never paste Claude/ChatGPT/Copilot CSS into the site.
- During recovery/health-limited sessions: one short step at a time; no restore roulette; no “fix every page” pressure.
